# Byte-determinism on the branch where bytes are the product.
#
# TR-BLD-002's stated reason is payload-specific: "a CRLF line ending in a JSON
# payload changes its bytes and therefore its content hash, silently breaking
# hash-gating on Windows checkouts". Those payloads live here, so the rule
# belongs here too. Without it, a checkout of this branch on a machine with
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites every published file on every run.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.json text eol=lf
